  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "13193718",
      "title": "Creating a Basic Attribute Directive",
      "lectureOrder": 417,
      "videoOrder": 384,
      "sourceHash": "d08a19f2331c226b6f4f5215f502184dd30adfde140572bb0b17699f75d58ec1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 4.38,
          "en": "-: So we already use attribute directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.38,
          "end": 6.45,
          "en": "like ngClass and ngStyle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.45,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "It's even easier to understand what to do once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "we've built our own one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "So I want to build a directive, which simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 16.02,
          "en": "highlights a element I hover over, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.02,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "Of course I could achieve the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 21.27,
          "en": "with normal CSS styles, but this is just a good demo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "So I will create a new folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "and I will name it basic highlight",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 27.743,
          "en": "like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.743,
          "end": 32.1,
          "en": "because in there I'll create a new file, basic highlight",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.1,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "and now directive.ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.95,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "So before we always had component files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 40.17,
          "en": "Now this is a new element, it's not a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.17,
          "end": 42.9,
          "en": "It will be a directive, hence the file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.9,
          "end": 46.503,
          "en": "Now in this file, I'll export a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.06,
          "end": 50.843,
          "en": "which will name BasicHighlightDirective.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "Again, to be descriptive about what this class is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 57.99,
          "en": "and to make it a directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.99,
          "end": 61.11,
          "en": "just like with a component where we added at component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.11,
          "end": 64.47,
          "en": "here we have to add at directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.47,
          "end": 68.88,
          "en": "And directive needs to be imported from at Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.88,
          "end": 71.07,
          "en": "So make sure to add this import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 73.2,
          "en": "and we need to pass an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 75.99,
          "en": "to this decorator to configure this directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.99,
          "end": 78.3,
          "en": "Now, how do we configure a directive?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "The one thing our directive absolutely needs is a selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 84.96000000000001,
          "en": "Because remember, we do place directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.96000000000001,
          "end": 88.32,
          "en": "in our template to attach them to elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.32,
          "end": 92.31,
          "en": "so we need to have some way to give Angular that instruction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.31,
          "end": 94.17,
          "en": "and that is the selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.17,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "Here, that should also be a unique selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "So typically here you use a camel case notation to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 106.05,
          "en": "give it appHighlight as a selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.05,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "or here maybe appBasicHighlight like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 113.58,
          "en": "Now that would select it by element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.58,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "Now I want to have this attribute style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 118.41,
          "en": "so I'm going to wrap this in square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.41,
          "end": 121.23,
          "en": "which means this will now be recognized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.23,
          "end": 123.72,
          "en": "whenever I add appBasicHighlight",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.72,
          "end": 127.08,
          "en": "without square brackets to an element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 129.21,
          "en": "Now to show this, we need to do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.21,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "which gives us some visual glue that this is working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "So the basic thing is, the most basic use case is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 138,
          "en": "we change, let's say, the background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138,
          "end": 141.63,
          "en": "of the element where we attach this directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.63,
          "end": 143.31,
          "en": "For this, we need to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.31,
          "end": 145.38,
          "en": "to the element the directive sits on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 148.95,
          "en": "And the cool thing is, Angular gives us this access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.95,
          "end": 150.21,
          "en": "We can inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.21,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "the element the directive sits on into this directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 156.75,
          "en": "and injection is something we'll take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.75,
          "end": 158.94,
          "en": "at in the next course module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.94,
          "end": 162.81,
          "en": "in the big next course module, which is about services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.81,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "I can say that much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 166.41,
          "en": "It basically is an easy way to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.41,
          "end": 167.88,
          "en": "to some other classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 171.57,
          "en": "without having them to instantiate on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.57,
          "end": 173.82,
          "en": "We do in check by adding the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.82,
          "end": 176.19,
          "en": "which every types of class has.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.19,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "We don't need to write anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 179.22,
          "en": "in the constructor body for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 180.51,
          "en": "But here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.51,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "on the list of arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 184.98,
          "en": "we list a couple of arguments you want to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 184.98,
          "end": 188.37,
          "en": "whenever an instance of this class here is created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 188.37,
          "end": 190.2,
          "en": "And of course Angular is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 191.91,
          "en": "for creating these instances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 191.91,
          "end": 193.62,
          "en": "So, therefore, if we tell it to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 196.5,
          "en": "please give us a specific type of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 196.5,
          "end": 199.05,
          "en": "argument, this is what injection is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 199.05,
          "end": 201.81,
          "en": "Angular will try to create this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 201.81,
          "end": 204.51,
          "en": "thing we need and give it to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.51,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "Well, this thing we need, in this case simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 212.4,
          "en": "is a reference to the element the directive was placed on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 212.4,
          "end": 215.52,
          "en": "So a element reference, this name is totally up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 215.52,
          "end": 217.23,
          "en": "but the type is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 217.23,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "The type has to be ElementRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 222.6,
          "en": "You might recognize this from at ViewChild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.6,
          "end": 225.57,
          "en": "There, it also was a reference to some element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.57,
          "end": 226.713,
          "en": "Here, it is two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "Now to be able to use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "data in our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 234.12,
          "en": "class here, everywhere in the class, we can use a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 234.12,
          "end": 237.66,
          "en": "TypeScript shortcut of adding private in front of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 237.66,
          "end": 239.43,
          "en": "which will make this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 239.43,
          "end": 241.98,
          "en": "both a property of this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 241.98,
          "end": 244.59,
          "en": "So property ElementRef and automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 244.59,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "assign this value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 249.54,
          "en": "So this instance, we're getting to this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 249.54,
          "end": 250.56,
          "en": "Now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 250.56,
          "end": 252.39,
          "en": "we got access to the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 255.33,
          "en": "Now we can use it here in our constructor, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 255.33,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "access to nativeElement and then do something with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 261.78,
          "en": "Though, a better place than the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 261.78,
          "end": 263.79,
          "en": "is OnInIt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 263.79,
          "end": 265.807,
          "en": "And just like the,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 265.807,
          "end": 268.137,
          "en": ",uh, component, the directive also has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 268.137,
          "end": 271.74,
          "en": "the ngOnInIt lifecycle hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 271.74,
          "end": 274.413,
          "en": "So, here I can therefore add ngOnInIt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 275.503,
          "end": 278.64,
          "en": "And in there we could access elementRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 278.64,
          "end": 280.86,
          "en": "that's the shortcut which automatically gave me this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 280.86,
          "end": 283.29,
          "en": "property, access to nativeElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 283.29,
          "end": 286.2,
          "en": "And there access the style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 286.2,
          "end": 289.8,
          "en": "and maybe the background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 289.8,
          "end": 291.57,
          "en": "and set this equal to green",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 291.57,
          "end": 294.03,
          "en": "so that we can see something changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 294.03,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "So what we're doing here is we're getting access to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 297.63,
          "en": "element, the directive was placed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 297.63,
          "end": 300.48,
          "en": "on getting access to that exact element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 300.48,
          "end": 302.97,
          "en": "And then we're overriding the style of this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 302.97,
          "end": 305.01,
          "en": "Now let's use this directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 305.01,
          "end": 307.92,
          "en": "To use it, we have to do two things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 307.92,
          "end": 310.29,
          "en": "First of all, like for a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 310.29,
          "end": 314.16,
          "en": "we have to inform Angular that we have a new directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 314.16,
          "end": 315.39,
          "en": "Just like with components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 315.39,
          "end": 317.49,
          "en": "it doesn't scan all our files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 317.49,
          "end": 319.08,
          "en": "so it doesn't know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 319.08,
          "end": 321.03,
          "en": "So we have to go to app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 321.03,
          "end": 323.58,
          "en": "and here in declarations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 323.58,
          "end": 326.94,
          "en": "we have to add our BasicHighlightDirective",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 328.08,
          "end": 331.56,
          "en": "and also add the import pointing to the basic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 331.56,
          "end": 332.4,
          "en": "highlight folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 335.90999999999997,
          "en": "and there to the BasicHighlightDirective file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 335.90999999999997,
          "end": 338.4,
          "en": "Now with this, we can use the directive in our app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 338.4,
          "end": 340.56,
          "en": "since we informed Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 340.56,
          "end": 343.83,
          "en": "Now let's use it in our app component HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 343.83,
          "end": 346.59000000000003,
          "en": "And here below all our lists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 346.59000000000003,
          "end": 348.96,
          "en": "I will simply add a new paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 348.96,
          "end": 352.8,
          "en": "style me with basic directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 352.8,
          "end": 354.33,
          "en": "something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 354.33,
          "end": 355.40999999999997,
          "en": "And now to this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 355.40999999999997,
          "end": 359.1,
          "en": "I can add appBasicHighlight, my own selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 359.1,
          "end": 361.02,
          "en": "We don't need to set any value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 361.02,
          "end": 364.23,
          "en": "And importantly we don't use square brackets",
